I have prepared the complete workspace updates and firmware for your Arduino Uno relay-controlled motor:

### ⚡ Wiring & Circuit Connections:
- **Relay Module**:
  - `VCC` -> Arduino `5V`
  - `GND` -> Arduino `GND`
  - `IN` -> Arduino `D7` (digital control)
- **DC Motor & Relay**:
  - Motor (+) -> External 5V Supply (+)
  - Motor (-) -> Relay `NO` (Normally Open terminal)
  - Relay `COM` -> External Supply Ground (`GND`)
  - External GND -> Arduino `GND` (shared reference)
  - 1N4007 Diode across Motor: Cathode (banded side) to Motor (+), Anode to Motor (-)

### 💻 Updated Firmware Sketch:
```cpp
#include <Arduino.h>

const int RELAY_PIN = 7;      // Digital control pin for relay module
const int STATUS_LED = 13;    // Built-in status LED

void setup() {
  // Drive LOW before configuring OUTPUT to avoid power-on trigger spikes
  digitalWrite(RELAY_PIN, LOW);
  pinMode(RELAY_PIN, OUTPUT);
  pinMode(STATUS_LED, OUTPUT);

  Serial.begin(115200);
  Serial.println("VoltForge: Relay Motor Controller Initialized");
}

void loop() {
  // Turn motor ON for 3 seconds
  Serial.println("Motor ON");
  digitalWrite(RELAY_PIN, HIGH);
  digitalWrite(STATUS_LED, HIGH);
  delay(3000);

  // Turn motor OFF for 3 seconds
  Serial.println("Motor OFF");
  digitalWrite(RELAY_PIN, LOW);
  digitalWrite(STATUS_LED, LOW);
  delay(3000);
}
```

You can apply these connections and code directly in your workspace!

### ⚡ Voltage Divider & Pin Connections for ESP32:
- `VCC` -> ESP32 `5V` (or Vin)
- `GND` -> ESP32 `GND`
- `TRIG` -> ESP32 `GPIO5`
- `ECHO` -> 10 kΩ Resistor -> ESP32 `GPIO18`
- ESP32 `GPIO18` -> 20 kΩ Resistor -> `GND`

### 💻 Complete ESP32 Distance Firmware:
```cpp
#include <Arduino.h>

const int TRIG_PIN = 5;
const int ECHO_PIN = 18;

void setup() {
  Serial.begin(115200);
  pinMode(TRIG_PIN, OUTPUT);
  pinMode(ECHO_PIN, INPUT);
  digitalWrite(TRIG_PIN, LOW);
  Serial.println("VoltForge: HC-SR04 Distance Sensor on ESP32 Ready");
}

void loop() {
  // Trigger a 10 microsecond HIGH pulse
  digitalWrite(TRIG_PIN, LOW);
  delayMicroseconds(2);
  digitalWrite(TRIG_PIN, HIGH);
  delayMicroseconds(10);
  digitalWrite(TRIG_PIN, LOW);

  // Measure the round-trip echo duration in microseconds
  long duration = pulseIn(ECHO_PIN, HIGH, 30000);

  if (duration == 0) {
    Serial.println("Out of range / No echo detected");
  } else {
    // Speed of sound is ~343 m/s = 0.0343 cm/us -> divide by 2 for one-way
    float distanceCm = (duration * 0.0343) / 2.0;
    Serial.print("Distance: ");
    Serial.print(distanceCm, 1);
    Serial.println(" cm");
  }

  delay(200);
}
```

